{
    "$comment": [
        "Merge these keys into the plugin's composer.json; this file is not a composer.json of its own.",
        "Versions are the current releases as of 2026-10-02 (repo.packagist.org).",
        "pestphp/pest ^3.8 runs on PHP 8.2 and later (PHPUnit 11). Raise it to ^4.7 (PHP 8.3, PHPUnit 12) when the suite's PHP is 8.3 or later. Do not raise it to ^5 while the plugin has an Integration suite: Pest 5 requires PHPUnit 13, and yoast/phpunit-polyfills 4.0.0, which the WordPress test suite requires, supports PHPUnit 7.5 to 9, 11 and 12 only.",
        "Do not pin config.platform.php to the supported floor. Tooling resolves on the developer's PHP; the floor belongs in require.php (Rector and PHPStan read it). Same rule as the code-quality skill. Keep an existing platform pin only when the repository already needs one for another reason (for example a test-toolchain pin).",
        "wp-phpunit/wp-phpunit follows WordPress' own versions. Pin it to the minor the installs run (wp core version), so the test library matches the core it boots.",
        "A plugin with no composer.json gets one holding these keys plus name, description, type and license, and a require block holding only php (the supported floor, which Rector and PHPStan read): development dependencies only, so nothing is installed into production."
    ],
    "require-dev": {
        "brain/monkey": "^2.7",
        "pestphp/pest": "^3.8",
        "wp-phpunit/wp-phpunit": "~7.1.0",
        "yoast/phpunit-polyfills": "^4.0"
    },
    "config": {
        "sort-packages": true,
        "allow-plugins": {
            "pestphp/pest-plugin": true
        }
    },
    "scripts": {
        "test": [
            "@test:unit",
            "@test:integration"
        ],
        "test:unit": "pest --testsuite=Unit",
        "test:integration": "pest --testsuite=Integration"
    },
    "scripts-descriptions": {
        "test": "Run both suites, each in its own process, so the Unit suite never sees WordPress.",
        "test:unit": "Run the suite that needs no WordPress and no database.",
        "test:integration": "Run the suite that boots WordPress through wp-phpunit against the test database."
    }
}
